SUMMARY:Aga Khan Museum: Labyrinth Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe will return to see **Labyrinth Ense
 mble** for the 6th time!\n\nhttps://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/labyrinth-e
 nsemble-with-geylan/\n\nEvery FOUR years\, the 14 members 'disband'\, and 
 a new group of 14 members is put together. A new cohort!\n\nThere will be 
 a "TURKISH' theme to this concert! With visiting guests.\n\nWhich also mea
 ns 14 new instruments to learn about!\n\nhttps://www.labyrinthontario.com/
 events\n\nThe new cohort will dig into European Medieval\, the Eastern Med
 iterranean\, the Middle East\, and Central Asian musical traditions\, and 
 will feature unique instrumentation ranging from guzheng\, Hardanger fiddl
 e\, lutes\, hurdy gurdy\, qanun and microtonal guitar\; bringing a whole n
 ew sound to the project.\n\nThe Aga Khan Museum concert hall is one of our
  top 3 spots in Toronto--for live music.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Purchase your own tic
 ket--**and the ticket price includes** entry into the Museum from 6pm onwa
 rds (which we always do). We can check out the new exhibitions.\nIf intere
 sted\, grab your own ticket. Don't miss out!\n\nA short video--3 of the 14
  members perform at local Thorncliffe Park festival last summer\n[https://
 www.youtube.com/watch?v=o2XjudW45nQ](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o2Xju
 dW45nQ)\n\nTickets have just gone 'on sale'. I've purchased a ticket in Ro
 w F.\n\nPrices are: $50 regular. $37.50 for Senior.\n\n**Ticket link here:
 **\n\nhttps://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/labyrinth-ensemble-with-geylan/
