SUMMARY:European Union Film Festival (EUFF):  Germany & Greece ($10-$12 ea
 ch)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n*We'll return to **EUFF**-Toronto\, fo
 r the 13th year!*\n\nExperience the richness of Europe through 28 outstand
 ing films. Each film is chosen by the Toronto Consulate of that country.\n
 \nWe'll see (just) 2 of them on Wednesday November 18th. If you cannot att
 end either one of these--then grab your friends are try and see another on
 e during the Festival.\n\n**6pm: Germany (Drama)**\n\nhttps://euffto.com/s
 inglefilmpage/impatience-of-the-heart/\n\n**8:30pm: Greece (Comedy)**\n\nh
 ttps://euffto.com/singlefilmpage/receptions/\n\n**NOTE:** You should purch
 ase your ticket in advance (I've done)\, or *take your chance* on a FREE R
 USH ticket. Keeping in mind--that these two Countries always have very pop
 ular films--within the local diaspora.\n\nEUFF suggestion is--IF you wish 
 to lineup on 'night of' for a FREE ticket--get there 60 minutes beforehand
 ...OR...just purchase a ticket in advance!\n\nYou may get a free RUSH tick
 et---or NOT.\n\nThe FULL schedule is here: (taking place over two weeks). 
 Two films each night.\n\nhttps://euffto.com/\n\n**EURO CAFE** returns and 
 is open (7:30pm-8:30pm only)\, for wine/food. Excellent wine and Mediterra
 nean treats.\n\nSpadina Theatre has 150 seats. General admission.\n\nWe ca
 n meet in advance (those with confirmed tickets and sit together)
